	(text "================================================================================\nCOMBO NODE SUBSYSTEM DESIGN & REVIEW NOTES (REV 3.6)\n================================================================================\nProject: OpenMycoNet COMBO_NODE\nSheet: /RESULT AND REVIEW/\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 3.6\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Solid GND Stackup)\n\n\n1. WATCHDOG SUPERVISOR STANDARDIZATION\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• Component & Value: TPS3851H33 (U7) timing capacitor C45 synchronized to 100 nF \n  across Schematic, PCB Layout, BOM, and CPL deliverables.\n• Timeout Period: Standardized to 323 ms nominal (tWD = 3.23 * 100nF + 0.381 ms) \n  across all engineering reports, eliminating false resets during active I2C/SPI \n  sensor acquisition cycles.\n\n\n2. INA333 BIO-SIGNAL ANALOG FRONT-END PROTECTION (U10 / CASE 3)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• Signal Flow Order: Terminal J4 -> Clamping Diodes D3 (BAV199DW) -> Series \n  Resistors R56/R57 -> INA333 (U10) Inputs.\n• Dual-Stage Rail Clamping: Ultra-low-leakage diode array D3 (BAV199DW) clamps \n  differential surge/ESD pulses directly to +3.3VA and GND prior to entering U10.\n• Current Limiting: Precision series resistors R56 & R57 (1 kΩ, 0.1%) restrict \n  residual fault currents below 5 mA.\n\n\n3. OPTICAL ILLUMINATION & PROBE INTERFACE (J5/J6 - LED_BANK / POINT 10)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• Off-Board LED Drivers: On-board LEDs migrated to 2-pin screw terminals J5 and J6 \n  (LED_BANK) for 470 nm optical probe connections.\n• Rail Selection & Current Limiting: Current-limiting resistors R59 and R60 (68 Ω, \n  0805, 1/8 W) connected directly to +BATT supply (instead of VDD / +3.3V) to \n  prevent digital supply sagging. Forward current fixed at ~16.2 mA @ 4.2 V BATT.\n• Low-Side Switching: Controlled by BSS138 N-channel MOSFETs (Q1, Q2) driven by \n  active-HIGH logic (LED_PWM1 / LED_PWM2 on GPIO11 / GPIO10) with 10 kΩ gate \n  pull-down resistors (R34, R37).\n\n\n4. SOIL MOISTURE POWER GATING (CASE 5)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• High-Side Load Switch: TPS22919DCKR (U18) controlled by GPIO41 (MOISTURE_SLEEP) \n  gates the MOISTURE_VDD supply rail at J9 Pin 1, eliminating 5 mA - 15 mA sensor \n  idle power drain during MCU deep sleep. Controlled Quick Output Discharge (QOD) \n  discharges bulk capacitor C47 (47 µF) via R58 (1 kΩ) to GND when disabled.\n• Bus Continuity: Precision ADC U14 (ADS1115) VDD remains powered on continuous \n  +3.3VA to keep the shared I2C bus active without ESD diode back-feeding.\n\n\n5. EC EXCITATION PATH & RC HARMONICS SUPPRESSION (CASE 4)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• Low-Pass Filtering: Passive RC filter R38 (1 kΩ) and C29 (10 nF) placed at U13 \n  non-inverting input (+INA / Pin 3) establishes a 15.9 kHz cutoff frequency.\n• Analog Front-End Shutdown: Buffer U13 (OPA2320S) shutdown pins (~SHDN1 / ~SHDN2) \n  tied to ANA_SHUT (GPIO42), driving the AFE into a < 1 µA standby state in deep sleep.\n\n\n6. 1.65 V MIDPOINT REFERENCE BUFFER & DISTRIBUTION (VMID_REFF / POINTS 06, 14)\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• Midpoint Divider: R43/R44 standardized to 100 kΩ filtered by C34 (100 nF) to GND,\n  providing a stable 1.65 V midpoint with minimal current draw (16.5 µA from +3.3VA).\n\n• Standalone Voltage Follower: Actively buffered by dedicated low-quiescent single op-amp\n  U19 (OPA333AIDBVR, SOT-23-5) configured as a 1:1 unity-gain follower. Pin 3 (+IN) connects to\n  C34, and Pin 4 (-IN) is shorted to Pin 1 (OUT). Pin 1 drives net VMID_REFF through R62\n  (22 Ω isolation resistor) with local decoupling C51 (100 nF to GND).\n\n• Stage Isolation: U13B is completely isolated from R62/VMID_REFF and reserved exclusively for the\n  EC probe receive amplifier, preventing soil-signal crosstalk during active EC stimulation.\n\nStar Reference Distribution: VMID_REFF cleanly distributed to:\n1) INA333 (U10) Pin 5 (REF) for mid-rail bi-directional output swing.\n2) Input bias offset network R32.\n3) High-value 10 MΩ bias return resistors R63 and R64.\n4) EC stimulation return path (J11 Pin 2 & bottom of R46).\n\n7. ON-BOARD THERMISTOR SCHEMATIC RETENTION & DNP RATIONALE (TH1 / POINT 12)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• Manufacturing Deliverables: TH1 footprint is designated Do Not Populate (DNP) \n  and explicitly excluded from the final Bill of Materials (BOM) and Pick & Place \n  (CPL) export files. JLCPCB manufacturing runs will leave TH1 unpopulated.\n• Primary 3-Wire Battery Topology: Standard 3-wire LiPo battery packs (connected \n  via J2) utilize an internal 10 kΩ pack NTC. Leaving TH1 unpopulated prevents \n  parallel resistance errors (~5 kΩ equivalent) on BQ24075 (U4) Pin 1 (TS) that \n  would cause false thermal faults and block charging.\n• Schematic Retention & Debugging: TH1 symbol is intentionally retained on the \n  schematic drawing to document hardware fallback options. During bench testing \n  or field deployment, if a 2-wire battery (lacking an internal NTC) is utilized, \n  TH1 can be manually hand-soldered onto the PCB pads to enable local thermal \n  protection without requiring a schematic or PCB revision.\n\n\n"
